    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/board-diagram-interchange.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Relationship first, visualisation later",
      "prov:value": "**One sentence, and it is the owner's:**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/board-diagram-interchange.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What follows, and it is four things rather than a preference",
      "prov:value": "**A note carries no `x`, no `y`, no `board`, no `position`** — for the same\nreason a BPMN task carries no coordinates. The owner said it directly: *\"it\nlives on top of notes, not data within notes\"*, and *\"notes exist lower down\nthan folio. make sure arrows correct.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/board-diagram-interchange.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A board declares what it SHOWS, and absent means everything",
      "prov:value": "That decision also answered a question nobody asked it. The owner later said\nevery harness above the floor *\"has a board filled with all contents\"*, and\n**\"filled with all contents\" turns out to be the absent filter** — so the\nminimal board and the total board are the same document."
    }
  ]
}
